nodes.body:
Still mergeable on current main, and the GPU run above remains the evidence for it.

Context that did not exist when I opened this. RFC #53194 has since pulled two other people onto this same invariant: @Tejasvichand and I split the conformance work, which is #53769, and @rishabhsinha17 has mapped the connector keying shapes out onto the external tiers (MooncakeStore, LMCache). This PR is the in-tree instance of the shape that gets it wrong. `ExampleConnector`, the reference disagg-prefill connector, re-derives its storage key from raw prompt tokens, so it will hand three full blocks of request A's KV to a request B that differs in `cache_salt` or LoRA, and it keys `prompt_embeds` requests on an empty prompt. Every `ExampleConnector` arm in #53769 is therefore a strict xfail today, and each one turns into a loud XPASS the moment this lands.

@russellb, could you apply the `ready` label so CI can actually report here? Outsider PRs get no run at all, so this has spent two weeks sitting on zero signal rather than on a disagreement with anything in it.

